Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(event‑level columns unless otherwise stated)

event_date:           filter to December 2020 tables (events_20201201 – events_20201231)  
event_name:           make sure we stay at the event grain, can be used for quick sanity checks  
event_params:         store every parameter; UNNEST() will be used  
 ‑ key               → look for 'session_engaged' and 'ga_session_id'  
 ‑ value.int_value   → value of the two parameters above (1 = “yes” for session_engaged)  
user_pseudo_id:       visitor identifier (part of the session key)  
ga_session_id (param): second half of the session key; must be extracted from event_params  
Conditions that will be applied  

• event_date like '202012%' (or use only the “events_202012**” tables)  
• key = 'session_engaged'                AND value.int_value = 1  
• key = 'ga_session_id'                  (to retrieve the session id)  

